title: Circuit Board
text: Light only runs along a trace, never across one. Follow the wiring, and drill a via wherever two traces meet.
trick: conduit traces carry each colour from pad to pad; red and blue traces cut across each other, so each beam needs a teleporter pair as a via to hop the other's trace
motif: a circuit board: conduit traces with gaps for pads, a red LED and a blue LED at the ends of their traces
ink: 4
expect: shared>=0
---
L 0 3 2 r
L 8 14 0 b
% red: along the top trace, down, via under blue, up to its LED
C 1 3 2 k
C 2 3 2 k
C 3 3 2 k
C 4 3 2 k
*R 5 3 7 k
C 5 4 0 k
C 5 5 0 k
C 5 6 0 k
C 5 7 0 k
*R 5 8 3 k
*x 7 8 0 k
*x 9 8 0 k
*R 10 8 1 k
C 10 7 0 k
C 10 6 0 k
C 10 5 0 k
C 10 4 0 k
T 10 2 0 ?
% blue: up its trace, west, via over red
C 8 13 0 k
